{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Simpleton: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja50'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 50 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Atthakāmavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Wanting to Help </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>10. Dummedhajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Simpleton: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Dummedhānaṁ sahassena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A sacrifice of simpletons by the thousand </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yañño me upayācito; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>was pledged by me. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Idāni khohaṁ yajissāmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Now I shall sacrifice </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bahu adhammiko jano”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>many an unrighteous man. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Dummedhajātakaṁ dasamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Atthakāmavaggo pañcamo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Atha mittaka mātu kapotavaro, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tathā veḷuka eḷamūgo rohiṇī; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kapi vāruṇi cetacarā ca puna, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tathā tāraka yaññavarena dasāti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Paṭhamo paṇṇāsako. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
